      "body": "`sgl-router/tests/scripts/generate_chat_render_parity.py` no longer imports:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom sglang.srt.entrypoints.openai import encoding_dsv4\r\nfrom sglang.srt.entrypoints.openai.chat_encoding import (\r\n    resolve_dsv4_reasoning_effort_profile,\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\ne22a530859 (\"openai: Render DeepSeek-V4/V4.1 chat prompts with deepseek-recipe\") deleted `encoding_dsv4.py` and `encoding_dsv41.py` and dropped `resolve_dsv4_reasoning_effort_profile` from `chat_encoding.py`. The same commit updated `rust/sglang-processor/tests/scripts/generate_parity.py`, which is the other copy of this generator, but the sgl-router copy kept the removed imports, so it now raises `ImportError` before rendering anything:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ python tests/scripts/generate_chat_render_parity.py\r\nImportError: cannot import name 'encoding_dsv4' from 'sglang.srt.entrypoints.openai'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat is the documented way to refresh `sgl-router/tests/fixtures/chat_render_parity/`, which `tests/component/tokenizer/render_parity.rs` checks against.\r\n\r\nThe `dsv4` branch now asks the serving adapter that the engine itself uses for the prompt, mirroring `_apply_jinja_template`, instead of re-deriving the renderer call inline. This also drops the local message normalisation the old branch duplicated (`pre_normalize` handles developer roles and object tool arguments, as the serving path does), and pins the adapter once per model rather than per case.\r\n\r\nThe Jinja models are untouched. I did not regenerate `deepseek-v4-flash.json` here because it needs the pinned checkpoint tokenizer; if the recipe render differs from the deleted encoder, that fixture will need a refresh too.\r\n\r\nChecked on a checkout of `main` (`25ba24e9a`): `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass on the file, and both imports resolve (`DeepSeekRecipeChatEncodingAdapter.__init__` and `encode_messages` take exactly the arguments passed here).\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
